ed in the  80s it was in the 80s to enter countries  in Europe and Saudi Arabia and his  lawyer said he had that for the reasons  of personal protection he  we wanted to hide the fact that he was  Jewish in case terrorists somehow  kidnapped him in the Middle East where  he was doing lots of business he says he  would turn over that passport as proof  that he wasn't Jeffrey Epstein he was  somebody who was not Jewish that's what  the lawyers argued in papers to the  judge and one of the things that you  mentioned before was how they're gonna  have a private guard with him a GPS  monitor why are they asking for that  well they were saying that would  guarantee that he would show up for the  hearing for the trial and of course bail  is only meant to make sure that you  guarantee the person will appear for the  hearing or if there's a possible risk or  a threat to the safety of the community  the judge also was given evidence that  he in the past had offered payments to  people who might be witnesses against  him and also the prosecutor said he  should not get special treatment just  because he's wealthy he shouldn't be  able to buy his own private jail and  what do we know about this trial going  forward do we know many details yet I  know this is obviously new today well  this is due today that means he'll be  sitting in the Metropolitan Correctional  Center in downtown Manhattan here in New  York City while he awaits his trial the  sex trafficking charges are very  extensive and prosecutors also presented  evidence they discovered when they went  through his safe at his mansion here in  New York finding hundreds if not  thousands of pictures of naked women  many of them they say were underage  women of course he was accused and  pleaded guilty to abusing dozens of  teenage girls in Florida and in New York  they also found 75 seventy thousand  dollars in cash a big quantity of  diamonds fraud diamonds one of them 2.3  eight carats so they were arguing that  given all